From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: hand queue submits to a serialized submitter

The scheduler worker must not remain inside a driver-facing queue submit. Hand
submissions to a serialized submitter so it can record later command chunks
while RADV is blocked, while direct present and sparse operations remain ordered.
Track the tick only after the driver accepts the submission; deferred fence
waits therefore remain unbounded without observing an unsubmitted tick.

---

--- a/src/common/hang_site.h
+++ b/src/common/hang_site.h
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 namespace Common {
 
 /// The threads whose place the hang watch reports.
-enum class HangThread : std::size_t { Back, Worker, Present, Fence, Count };
+enum class HangThread : std::size_t { Back, Worker, Present, Fence, Submitter, Count };
 
 /// EDEN_NX2_HANG_WATCH=1. A function-local static: env.txt is read in main, after the globals.
 [[nodiscard]] inline bool HangWatchOn() {
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
